# Local-only defaults for the two connection fields on the Settings screen.
#
# To use: copy this file to `config/.env` (same folder, drop the `.example`) and fill
# in your values. The app reads it at startup and prefills the fields; it never
# connects on its own, and a config you have already saved in the browser wins.
#
# `config/.env` is gitignored and must stay that way. The hosted site has no such
# file — there you type both values into Settings by hand.
#
# Neither value is a secret. The OAuth Client ID is public by design: it is visible
# in the browser either way. The Spreadsheet ID names a document without granting
# access to it — reading the Sheet still requires signing in as someone it is shared
# with. They are kept out of git because they identify *your* setup, not because they
# unlock anything.
#
# No financial data belongs in this file. Only the two keys below are read; anything
# else here is ignored.

# Google Cloud Console -> Credentials -> your OAuth 2.0 Client ID (type: Web application)
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# From your Sheet's URL: docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS PART>/edit
SPREADSHEET_ID=
